      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Economic sanctions are a blunt instrument that often fail to achieve their stated goal of spreading democracy while instead serving as a tool for geopolitical bullying. History shows that prolonged pressure on smaller nations frequently leads to authoritarian hardening rather than reform, as regimes use isolation to consolidate power and suppress dissent. Instead of forcing change, these measures often deepen economic suffering among ordinary citizens without compelling the leadership to relinquish control.",
